#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:1
msgid "Derivation \"ATerm\" file format"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:3
msgid ""
"For historical reasons, [store derivations](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation) are stored on-disk in \"Annotated Term\" (ATerm) format ([guide]"
"(https://homepages.cwi.nl/~daybuild/daily-books/technology/aterm-guide/aterm-"
"guide.html), [paper](https://doi.org/10.1002/"
"(SICI)1097-024X(200003)30:3%3C259::AID-SPE298%3E3.0.CO;2-Y))."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:7
msgid ""
"Only a small fragment of ATerm is used: the constructors below, string "
"literals, lists, and tuples."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:9
msgid "The ATerm format used"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:11
msgid "Derivations are serialised in one of the following formats:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:17
msgid "For all stable derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:23
msgid ""
"The only `version-string`s that are in use today are for [experimental "
"features](../development/experimental-features.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:25
msgid ""
"`\"xp-dyn-drv\"` for the [`dynamic-derivations`](../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-dynamic-derivations) experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:27
msgid "Grammar"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:29
msgid ""
"```ebnf\n"
"derivation = \"Derive(\" fields \")\"\n"
"           | \"DrvWithVersion(\" version \",\" fields \")\" ;\n"
"\n"
"fields = outputs \",\" input-drvs \",\" input-srcs \",\"\n"
"         platform \",\" builder \",\" args \",\" env ;\n"
"\n"
"outputs    = \"[\" [ output { \",\" output } ] \"]\" ;\n"
"output     = \"(\" output-name \",\" output-path \",\" hash-algo \",\" hash "
"\")\" ;\n"
"\n"
"input-drvs = \"[\" [ input-drv { \",\" input-drv } ] \"]\" ;\n"
"input-drv  = \"(\" drv-path \",\" input-drv-node \")\" ;\n"
"\n"
"input-srcs = \"[\" [ store-path { \",\" store-path } ] \"]\" ;\n"
"\n"
"builder    = string ;\n"
"args       = \"[\" [ string { \",\" string } ] \"]\" ;\n"
"\n"
"env        = \"[\" [ env-entry { \",\" env-entry } ] \"]\" ;\n"
"env-entry  = \"(\" string \",\" string \")\" ;\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:51
msgid "The leaves are all double-quoted, but fall into two kinds."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:53
msgid ""
"```ebnf\n"
"(* may contain escape sequences *)\n"
"string      = '\"' { char | escape } '\"' ;\n"
"\n"
"(* drawn from restricted alphabets, so never escaped *)\n"
"verbatim    = '\"' { char } '\"' ;\n"
"\n"
"(* Not an alternation but a parameter of the grammar: the store\n"
"   directory fixes which one holds, for the whole file at once.\n"
"   See the note below. *)\n"
"store-path  = ? verbatim under a Unix store directory,\n"
"                string under a Windows one ? ;\n"
"\n"
"drv-path    = store-path ; (* a store path whose name ends in \".drv\" *)\n"
"output-path = store-path | '\"\"' ;\n"
"output-name = verbatim ;\n"
"platform    = verbatim ;\n"
"version     = verbatim ;\n"
"\n"
"hash-algo     = '\"' [ method-prefix ] algorithm '\"' | '\"\"' ;\n"
"method-prefix = \"r:\" | \"text:\" | \"git:\" ;      (* flat has none *)\n"
"algorithm     = \"blake3\" | \"md5\" | \"sha1\" | \"sha256\" | \"sha512\" ;\n"
"\n"
"hash        = '\"' hex-digit { hex-digit } '\"' | '\"\"' | '\"impure\"' ;\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:79
msgid ""
"A `store-path` is a [store path](../protocols/store-path.md) written in "
"full, store directory included."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:81
msgid ""
"Note that the derivation _name_ does not appear anywhere. It is taken from "
"the store path of the derivation, and so must be supplied out-of-band; see "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:84
#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:186
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:86
msgid ""
"`store-path` is the one leaf that is not pinned down by the grammar, and the "
"reason is the store directory. A Unix one, `/nix/store`, happens to hold no "
"character the format escapes, so the path can be written verbatim. A Windows "
"one does: `C:\\ProgramData\\nix\\store` contains backslashes, which must be "
"escaped, making the leaf a `string`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:90
msgid ""
"```\n"
"\"C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\nix\\\\store/ib3sh3pcz10wsmavxvkdbayhqivbghlq-foo\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:94
msgid ""
"Only the store directory is affected; the `/` separating it from the rest of "
"the path is a forward slash either way. Nothing else moves: `output-name`, "
"`platform`, `version` and the two hash fields are drawn from alphabets that "
"never need escaping, whichever store directory is in use."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:97
msgid ""
"This is a mode, not a choice made afresh at each store path: one of the two "
"holds throughout a given file, and every store path in it is written that "
"way. The mode is not recorded in the file and cannot be recovered from the "
"bytes — a verbatim path is also a well-formed `string` — so it has to be "
"supplied out of band, like the derivation name. Nix takes it from the store "
"it is reading or writing for, defaulting to the platform it was built for, "
"and then holds the parser to it: under a Unix store directory a store path "
"carrying an escape is _rejected_ rather than accepted as a second spelling "
"of the same path. That is what keeps the encoding [canonical](#canonical-"
"form) in either case."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:102
msgid "Strings"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:104
msgid ""
"Every leaf above is a double-quoted string. Within one, `\"` and `\\` are "
"escaped with a backslash, and newline, carriage return, and tab are written "
"`\\n`, `\\r`, and `\\t`. Those five are the only escapes there are, and each "
"of those five characters is only ever written escaped; see [canonical form]"
"(#canonical-form)."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:108
msgid ""
"Fields drawn from restricted alphabets — output names, the platform, and the "
"hash fields — cannot contain any of them, and so are written verbatim. Store "
"paths are written verbatim too, unless the store directory itself needs "
"escaping; see the note above."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:111
msgid "Outputs"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:113
msgid ""
"Which sort of output is meant is not tagged; it is inferred from which of "
"the three fields are empty."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:115
msgid "`output-path`"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:115
msgid "`hash-algo`"
msgstr ""

