#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:136
msgid ""
"`hash` is lowercase, and carries no algorithm prefix of its own — the "
"algorithm is named by `hash-algo`."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:138
msgid ""
"For a fixed-output derivation the `output-path` is redundant — it is a "
"function of the content address — but it must still agree with it. Two "
"derivations that mean the same thing would otherwise have different "
"encodings, and so different store paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:141
msgid "Input derivations"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:143
msgid ""
"Each entry pairs the store path of an input derivation with the outputs of "
"it that are used:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:145
msgid ""
"```ebnf\n"
"input-drv-node = output-names ;\n"
"output-names   = \"[\" [ output-name { \",\" output-name } ] \"]\" ;\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:150
msgid ""
"In the `DrvWithVersion(\"xp-dyn-drv\", ...)` form — which requires the "
"[`dynamic-derivations`](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-"
"dynamic-derivations) experimental feature — a node may instead nest, to name "
"an output of a derivation that is _itself_ an output of a derivation:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:154
msgid ""
"```ebnf\n"
"input-drv-node = output-names\n"
"               | \"(\" output-names \",\" \"[\" [ child { \",\" child } ] \"]"
"\" \")\" ;\n"
"child          = \"(\" output-name \",\" input-drv-node \")\" ;\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:160
msgid "Canonical form"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:162
msgid ""
"The encoding is meant to be canonical: each derivation has exactly one. This "
"matters because the bytes are hashed, both to content-address the derivation "
"itself and to compute [input-addressed](../protocols/store-path.md) output "
"paths, so two spellings of the same derivation would be two different "
"derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:165
msgid "Accordingly:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:167
msgid ""
"Outputs, input derivations, input sources, and environment variables appear "
"in ascending order of their keys, with no duplicates. The same holds of the "
"`output-names` naming which outputs of an input derivation are used."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:170
msgid ""
"A character that can be escaped must be escaped, and no other escape "
"sequence is valid. Both halves matter: a literal newline byte inside a "
"string, and `\\q`, are each a second way to write something that already has "
"a spelling."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:173
msgid ""
"The fields drawn from restricted alphabets — output names and the platform — "
"contain no escape sequences at all, since an escape there would be a second "
"encoding of the same value rather than a necessary one. Store paths are held "
"to the same rule, except where the store directory needs escaping, in which "
"case the escapes are the necessary kind."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:176
msgid ""
"Store paths are written in their canonical form, and the key of an "
"`inputDrvs` entry is a derivation path, ending in `.drv`."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:178
msgid "There is no trailing content after the closing parenthesis."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:180
msgid ""
"One exception is known. The JSON held in the [`__json` environment variable]"
"(../store/derivation/index.md#structured-attrs) of a derivation using "
"structured attributes is _not_ required to be canonical JSON. It must "
"instead be preserved verbatim rather than reserialised. Since the bytes are "
"hashed, whatever encoding a derivation happens to carry is part of its "
"identity. Re-emitting it — even as equivalent JSON — would change the "
"derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:188
msgid ""
"This is not because canonicity is unwanted here, but because there is no "
"settled notion of it to require. \"Canonical JSON\" has several competing "
"definitions, disagreeing on key ordering, number representation, and Unicode "
"escaping. It is also technically fraught: for example, without hex literals "
"for floating point, number representation is barely tractable. Structured "
"attributes have been in the wild for many years, so any such choice would "
"also have to reckon with the encodings already out there. Committing to one "
"of them is therefore not a choice we are yet in a position to make with this "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:195
msgid "Masked derivations"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:197
msgid ""
"An [input-addressed](../store/derivation/outputs/input-address.md) output "
"path is computed by hashing the ATerm representation of a derivation that "
"has been [masked](../store/derivation/outputs/input-address.md#input-masked-"
"drv) first: parts of it are blanked out before hashing, so that derivations "
"differing only in what was blanked hash alike."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:199
msgid "Their encoding differs from the grammar above in two productions:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:201
msgid ""
"```ebnf\n"
"masked-derivation   = \"Derive(\" fields \")\" ;\n"
"\n"
"input-drv           = \"(\" drv-hash \",\" output-names \")\" ;\n"
"drv-hash            = verbatim ;   (* lowercase hexadecimal *)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:208
msgid "That is:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:210
msgid ""
"There is no version header. A masked derivation is only ever constructed "
"once dynamic derivations have been resolved away, so it never needs one, and "
"`DrvWithVersion(...)` does not occur."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:213
msgid ""
"An `inputDrvs` key is a hash rather than a store path, and its node is "
"always the flat `output-names` — the nested form the `dynamic-derivations` "
"version allows cannot appear, for the same reason."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:215
msgid ""
"See [input addressing](../store/derivation/outputs/input-address.md#input-"
"masked-drv) for how those hashes are derived and why; in short, they "
"identify an input derivation up to what it produces rather than how, so that "
"changing where a fixed-output input is fetched from does not change anything "
"downstream."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:217
msgid ""
"Replacing the input derivation paths with hashes like this is _input "
"masking_, and is performed on all derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:219
msgid ""
"Whether the outputs carry their paths depends on what is being hashed. When "
"computing a derivation's own output paths they are _output masked_ too — "
"`output-path`, and the environment variable named after each output, are "
"empty — since those paths are what is being computed; the result is _fully "
"masked_. When hashing a derivation to stand in for it as an _input_ to "
"another, they are left as they are, and the result is _input-masked_ only."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:223
msgid ""
"The result is not a derivation that can be built, written to the store, or "
"read back by `parse`: its inputs name hashes, not paths. It exists only to "
"be hashed."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:226
msgid "Use for encoding to store object"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:228
msgid ""
"When derivation is encoded to a [store object](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"object) we make the following choices:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:230
msgid ""
"The store path [name](../store/store-path.md#name) is the derivation name "
"with `.drv` suffixed at the end"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:232
msgid ""
"Indeed, the ATerm format above does _not_ contain the name of the "
"derivation, on the assumption that a store path will also be provided out-of-"
"band."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:234
msgid ""
"The derivation is content-addressed using the [\"Text\" method](../store/"
"store-object/content-address.md#method-text) of content-addressing "
"derivations"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/derivation-aterm.md:236
msgid ""
"Currently we always encode derivations to store object using the ATerm "
"format (and the previous two choices), but we reserve the option to encode "
"new sorts of derivations differently in the future."
msgstr ""
